# The secure nets (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "The radio"): a Radio Operator who has cracked a faction's net
# (RZ_SecureRadio) and calls on a radio can talk on it too. An intruder's words go to the net, never
# to the air: nothing here is public. A lie that's caught costs the lie's Infamy as anywhere, and they
# change codes on you (the listening ends). Nobody names you on a net: you're a station, not a person.
# Secure channels are blunt, with numbers in them (docs/WRITING.md, "The voices").

conv radio.bastion.net
for radio:bastion
topic "Bastion, radio check. Over."
prio world
voice bastion

node start
  say Station calling, Bastion. Weak but readable. All stations: the roll at the shift change, the night watch at twenty-thirty. Nothing heard from Command in {days_since_command} days. Over.
  > @word Post four. Say again the word. Over. -> word | lost   check lie bastion 3   truth tier:bastion>=trusted
  > @listen Keep quiet and listen. -> listen
  > @off Switch off. -> hub

node word
  say Four, Bastion. Same word as at half five, and you had it then. Don't make me say it twice on a set the crews can hear. Out.
  do call:net_word
  > @back1 Copy. Out. -> hub

node lost
  say Post four is on the other set, whoever you are. All stations, Bastion: change to the spare frequency, now. Out.
  do call:net_lost
  > @back2 Bastion? Bastion, say again. -> hub

node listen
  say? night :: Post two, Bastion. Movement at the treeline, two hundred metres, six or seven. Holding fire: they're only walking. Will advise. Over.
  say? mood:grim :: Bastion, post three. Strength as last reported, less one. Rations, one day. Requesting the truck by morning. Over.
  say Post three, Bastion. Patrol out at the shift change, four names, back by dark. Log it. Out.
  > @back3 Switch off. -> hub

conv radio.redhand.net
for radio:redhand
topic "Evening, lads. Who's on?"
prio world
voice redhand

node start
  say Doesn't matter who's on, it's the boss's channel, so listen. Lorry at the crossroads, fifteen in the tin. Bridge, ten. Who's short? Nobody's short. Lovely. Keep it that way.
  > @toll Crew here. What's the toll today? -> toll | lost   check lie redhand 2   truth crew
  > @listen Keep quiet and listen. -> listen
  > @off Switch off. -> hub

node toll
  say Same as yesterday and the same tomorrow: the book says what you owe, and the lorry says what you pay. Why are you asking me on this? Write it on your hand. Out.
  do learn:redhand.toll
  > @back1 Cheers. Out. -> hub

node lost
  say That's not one of mine. Somebody's on the channel, lads, listening to every word. Swap it. Swap it now, and somebody find out who sold it!
  do call:net_lost
  > @back2 Hello? Anyone? -> hub

node listen
  say? mood:hope :: If the cure's real, the price of everything goes up. Tins, fuel, a seat on a lorry to the checkpoints. Start writing bigger numbers in the book.
  say Book says the bridge crew's owed three days of their cut. Book's always right. Pay the bridge crew before they start counting out loud.
  > @back3 Switch off. -> hub

conv radio.halcyon.net
for radio:halcyon
topic "Lab, this is field. Radio check."
prio world
voice halcyon

node start
  say Field station, the lab. Read you. All field stations: sample intake is below target for the third shift running. The director requests patience, and samples. Lab out.
  > @count Station two. Say again the count. -> count | lost   check lie halcyon 2   truth tier:halcyon>=trusted
  > @listen Keep quiet and listen. -> listen
  > @off Switch off. -> hub

node count
  say Station two, the lab. {cure_percent} percent as of the change of shift. Samples wanted at the gate. Please do not round it up on the open channel. Lab out.
  do learn:halcyon.count
  > @back1 Copy. Station two out. -> hub

node lost
  say There is no station two on today's schedule. Noted, and logged with the time. All stations, change to the backup schedule now. Lab out.
  do call:net_lost
  > @back2 Lab? Lab, say again. -> hub

node listen
  say Station one, the lab. Overnight: volunteer seven is comfortable. Volunteer eight is comfortable. Notebooks to the lab by the change of shift. Out.
  > @back3 Switch off. -> hub
